# Copy this file to .env for local development.
#
# 1) Anthropic key — SERVER-SIDE ONLY (no VITE_ prefix), so it never ships to the browser.
#    The Express server (server.js) and its /api/claude proxy read this.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_key_here

# 2) Postgres (Render). Connection string from your Render Postgres dashboard
#    ("External Database URL"). Leave blank for quick local use (per-browser email+password,
#    no accounts). Render requires SSL; if you point at a LOCAL Postgres, set PGSSL=off.
DATABASE_URL=
# PGSSL=off                          # uncomment only for a local non-SSL Postgres

# 3) Auth — the secret used to sign/verify login JWTs. Generate a long random string:
#    node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('hex'))"
#    Required for real accounts; must be the SAME value everywhere the server runs.
AUTH_JWT_SECRET=
# JWT_ISS=karma-connect              # optional; issuer stamped into tokens (default shown)

# 4) Email confirmation (internal mail gateway) — OPTIONAL. If GATEWAY_URL + GATEWAY_TOKEN
#    are set, new signups must click an emailed link before they can sign in. If left blank,
#    accounts are created already-confirmed (no email step) — convenient for local dev.
#    The gateway holds the Resend key server-side; this app just POSTs to ${GATEWAY_URL}/send
#    with its per-client bearer token. Ask an admin for the token and to allowlist MAIL_FROM.
GATEWAY_URL=
GATEWAY_TOKEN=                          # per-client bearer token (keep out of source control)
MAIL_FROM=Karma Connect <karmaconnect@karmastaff.com>   # must be allowlisted for this token
# APP_URL=https://karma-connect-9s2z.onrender.com        # base URL used in the email link;
#                                                          if unset, derived from the request

# --- Rate limiting + token quotas + response cache (optional but recommended for production) ---
# Create a free Upstash Redis DB -> copy the REST URL + token:
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://xxx.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=...
# Tunables (optional, defaults shown):
# RATE_LIMIT_RPM=20                  # requests per user per minute
# DAILY_TOKEN_BUDGET=2000000         # tokens per user per day
# RESPONSE_CACHE_TTL=600             # seconds to cache identical requests
# BREAKER_FAILS=12                   # upstream failures/min before the global circuit breaker opens
# BREAKER_COOLDOWN=30                # seconds the breaker stays open
#
# Sign-up is OPEN by default: anyone who creates an account can use the app.
# To LOCK IT DOWN (recommended for a public URL — protects your API billing),
# set ONE of these on the server and only matching users are allowed:
# ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAIN=karmastaff.com               # only this email domain
# ALLOWED_EMAILS=a@karmastaff.com,b@karmastaff.com  # exact list (overrides the domain)

# Admins who can approve leads to unlock the Relationship / Meeting / Follow-up engines.
# Anyone NOT on this list is a normal member (free to use Hub + Intelligence + Connection,
# but the advanced engines stay locked per lead until an admin approves). Comma-separated.
# ADMIN_EMAILS=owner@karmastaff.com,manager@karmastaff.com

# Alternative way to grant admin: a secret code people can enter in the optional "Admin code"
# field on the signup screen. Correct code -> that new account is an admin; blank -> member.
# Share it privately only with people who should be admins. Leave unset to disable.
# ADMIN_SIGNUP_CODE=choose-a-long-secret-code
#
# Local dev port for the backend (Vite proxies /api here). Render sets PORT itself.
# PORT=8787
